# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Every entry here is something this project actually produces, or a
# costly accident worth guarding against. Boilerplate for toolchains this
# project does not use (packaging builds, Jython, HTML coverage reports)
# was removed deliberately - an ignore rule for a file that can never
# appear only makes the real ones harder to find.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS ───
# venv_gpu/ is the documented env (README "Setup"); .venv/ is what
# `uv sync` creates. Never commit either: gigabytes of platform-specific
# binaries that every machine has to build for itself anyway.
venv_gpu/
.venv/

# Not used today, and there are no secrets in this repository (see
# SECURITY.md) - kept because committing one costs far more than this line.
.env

# ─── PYTHON / TOOL CACHES ───
# All regenerated automatically; none of it is source.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# pytest-cov: `.coverage` locally (tools/check.py --full), `coverage.xml`
# in CI (--cov-report=xml).
.coverage
coverage.xml

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TRAINING ARTIFACTS  —  the big one
#
# These were previously untracked by accident rather than by design, which
# is how ~90MB of old checkpoint .zip files ended up permanently baked into
# git history across the "Update5/6/7/8" commits. Checkpoints are large
# binaries that change on every run and are already managed by
# train_agent.py, not by git.
#
# Note on order: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so the negation below only works because the master checkpoint
# lives at the repo root, not inside checkpoints/.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
checkpoints/
logs/
mario_brain_*checkpoint*.zip

# EXCEPTION: the master checkpoint IS tracked, so a fresh clone gets a
# working trained agent instead of an untrained random policy. At 20MB
# that is a reasonable one-off cost - but do NOT re-commit it after every
# retrain: git stores a near-complete new copy each time, which is exactly
# how this repo got bloated before. Commit an updated brain deliberately,
# when there is a real improvement worth sharing.
!mario_brain_checkpoint.zip

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EXPLORATION / QA ARTIFACTS
# exploration_data/ generated masks, jump arcs and bootstrap coverage
# checkpoints_qa/   the QA-phase model zips + their paired coverage, and
#                   final_objective2_16000000/ - the Objective-2 closure
#                   record, evidence and a backup of the main brain
#                   (their SHA-256s ARE tracked, in artifacts.json)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
exploration_data/
checkpoints_qa/

# Tool outputs - regenerable records, one per run:
#   coverage_audits/     tools/remaining_coverage_map.py (pictures + region lists)
#   evaluation/results/  tools/evaluate_completion.py and verify_level1.py
#   calibration_runs/    tools/calibrate_phase_reward.py (per-step pickles)
# evaluation/completion_baseline_6M.json sits OUTSIDE results/ on purpose: it
# is the frozen baseline, tracked and hash-protected, not a run output.
coverage_audits/
evaluation/results/
calibration_runs/

# Incident evidence bundles (Objective 3; reporting/store.py): screenshots,
# GIFs, reports and replays, one folder per incident. Runtime evidence, not
# source - kept locally, read-only, and served by the dashboard.
incidents/

# Release assets built by `python tools/final_brain.py bundle` (the final
# 16M brain bundle is published as a GitHub Release asset, never committed).
dist/

# The QA-phase master lives at the repo root, next to (never on top of)
# mario_brain_checkpoint.zip. Unlike that file it is NOT tracked: the
# completion brain is tracked so a fresh clone can watch the agent play, and
# the QA brain would add a new 20MB blob to history on every push.
glitch_hunter_qa.zip
glitch_hunter_qa_coverage.npz

# THE MAIN BRAIN: the approved 16,000,000-step Objective-2 brain and its
# coverage, renamed from the QA milestone on 2026-09-24. Not tracked for the
# same 20MB reason; its SHA-256s are in artifacts.json.
glitch_hunter_main_brain.zip
glitch_hunter_main_brain_coverage.npz

# ─── EDITORS & OS ───
# CI runs on Windows and Linux and CONTRIBUTING.md invites contributors, so
# the common per-machine droppings stay listed.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOT IGNORED, ON PURPOSE - listed here so nobody "helpfully" adds them:
#   uv.lock                     - the lockfile; committing it is what makes
#                                 `uv sync` reproducible for your friend.
#   static/vendor/              - the vendored socket.io client. It is a
#                                 dependency we deliberately ship so the
#                                 dashboard works with no internet.
#   mario_brain_checkpoint.zip  - see the exception above.
#   artifacts.json              - the SHA-256 of every protected artifact,
#                                 including ones that are themselves ignored.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
